{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-9-22","kind":"proposition","title":"性质与证明：整数","englishTitle":"If as many odd numbers as we please be added together, and their multitude be even, the whole will be even.","book":9,"number":22,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.22","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.22/","group":"prop","sourceNumber":22,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-9-22@raw-166fa02d7510b53d","contentId":"euclid-9-22","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"166fa02d7510b53dd23e92baf1286b9f6eb6f116d9bcd6d3ee3ae39b731d5cb2","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-9-22.statement","euclid-9-22.construction.1","euclid-9-22.proof.1","euclid-9-22.proof.2","euclid-9-22.conclusion","euclid-9-22.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-9-22.statement","contentId":"euclid-9-22","revisionId":"euclid-9-22@raw-166fa02d7510b53d","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"69888f523a989198ee6e9c5e9d7f009c55ba0ae4856da137140adb40b267667d","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"If as many odd numbers as we please be added together, and their multitude be even, the whole will be even."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果能把我们想要的 奇数加在一起 数量是公平的 整个数字是公平的"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-22.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-9-22","revisionId":"euclid-9-22@raw-166fa02d7510b53d","order":1,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"295e27744ed975ffc7cad852cc1abd5797e0bdad182abc8d46f019a24e8a010d","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For let as many odd numbers as we please, AB, BC, CD, DE, even in multitude, be added together; I say that the whole AE is even."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"不论我们多想多少奇数,都把AB、BC、CD、DE,甚至包括众多数字,加在一起;我说,整个AE是均衡的。"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-22.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-9-22","revisionId":"euclid-9-22@raw-166fa02d7510b53d","order":2,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"f249997c4411fe7204cecd0c152493c8116524c44542bfadbc82056bd59b319b","citations":["euclid-7-def-7","euclid-9-21"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, since each of the numbers AB, BC, CD, DE is odd, if an unit be subtracted from each, each of the remainders will be even; [[VII. Def. 7](/principles/euclid-7-def-7)] so that the sum of them will be even. [[IX. 21](/principles/euclid-9-21)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因为AB、BC、CD、DE等数字中的每一数字都是奇怪的,如果每数字减去单位,那么其余的每一个数字都是公平的;这样,两者的总数将是公平的。 [[VII. Def. 7](/principles/euclid-7-def-7)] [[IX. 21](/principles/euclid-9-21)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-22.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-9-22","revisionId":"euclid-9-22@raw-166fa02d7510b53d","order":3,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"5b55cf2970b889c12d96600f23237b1831badd728559bfa16ab19366b014f767","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But the multitude of the units is also even."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但单位的众多也算扯平了"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-22.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-9-22","revisionId":"euclid-9-22@raw-166fa02d7510b53d","order":4,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"546114959e91060294f43f0bf22516b85ad9ab11d58b81e88a6d7a2ebfb0a2fb","citations":["euclid-9-21"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore the whole AE is also even. [[IX. 21](/principles/euclid-9-21)] Q. E. D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,整个AE案件也是QE案件。 [[IX. 21](/principles/euclid-9-21)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-22.source","contentId":"euclid-9-22","revisionId":"euclid-9-22@raw-166fa02d7510b53d","order":5,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"58a0b37d8ba2ca41fb98bbe93327eb8af3c307bf7cd41f5bd93f19535a533b48","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.22/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.22\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-9-22:euclid-7-def-7:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-9-22","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-9-22.proof.1"],"targetContentId":"euclid-7-def-7","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.22","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.22/","sourceLabel":"VII. Def. 7"}},{"id":"edge:euclid-9-22:euclid-9-21:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-9-22","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-9-22.proof.1","euclid-9-22.conclusion"],"targetContentId":"euclid-9-21","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUr